  "summary_en": "European Commission's 2021 proposal replacing the Machinery Directive 2006/42/EC with a Regulation. It addresses risks from cobots, autonomous machinery, AI, software updates and cybersecurity, aligns with the New Legislative Framework, mandates third-party assessment for high-risk machinery including AI safety software, and coordinates with the AI Act.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Converts Machinery Directive into directly applicable Regulation aligned with the New Legislative Framework",
   "Safety components expressly include software; machinery missing only a software upload counts as machinery",
   "Introduces 'substantial modification' (physical or digital); modifier becomes manufacturer",
   "High-risk machinery list (Annex I) includes AI-based safety software requiring third-party conformity assessment",
   "Machinery with AI: AI Act requirements checked within machinery conformity assessment; new EHSRs on cybersecurity, autonomous behaviour and human-machine contact"
